@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Start a planned sprint
actor "Authorized user" as actor
box "Frontend - Mission Control application" #E0F2FE
  participant "SprintsPage, SprintPlanningPage or SprintBoardPage\nStartSprintDialog / SprintStartView" as page
  participant "ISprintService / SprintService" as client
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Api" #D1FADF
  participant "CurrentAccountAuthorization" as access
  participant "SprintsController" as ctrl
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "ValidationBehavior" as validation
  participant "StartSprintCommandHandler" as handler
  participant "Sprint" as entity
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Mission Control SQL" as db
end box
group Open the dialog (read on open)
  actor -> page : Start on a planned sprint: startRequested(sprintId), planning page Start sprint,\nor the board's No active sprint Start; StartSprintDialog opens with the sprint ID
  page -> client : sprintPlanResource(GetSprintPlanQuery): name, goal, dates, member count and points, version;\nno active-sprint check on open, so the dialog always opens on the confirmation
  client --> page : Start sprint disabled until it resolves (loading); a failed read shows Try again (reload) and Cancel,\nwith the reference ID only after a 500 (load-failed); a 404 emits notFound: the dialog closes with Outdated\nand the opening page rereads
end
actor -> page : Confirm Start sprint in StartSprintDialog
page -> client : Build typed StartSprintCommand with expected sprint version
client -> access : POST /api/workspaces/{id}/sprints/{sprintId}/start
access -> access : L2-002 validate signature, issuer, audience, subject, expiry
access -> db : Read current status, role and credential version
db --> access : Current account access
alt Missing, invalid or expired JWT; deactivated account
  access --> client : 401; audit denial without payloads
  client --> page : SessionService.end(Unauthorized) once; sign in with the Sprints tab as return route
else Authenticated (profile P: every active role starts sprints)
  access -> ctrl : Authorized request
  ctrl -> validation : Send StartSprintCommand through MediatR 12.5.0
  validation -> validation : Validate the expected version (path IDs already matched {id:guid})
  alt Missing or malformed expected version
    validation --> ctrl : 400 field error; nothing read or changed
    ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails
    client --> page : The alert shows the message without Retry or reference ID; Start sprint unavailable;\nfocus moves to the alert; sprint stays planned
  else Valid request
    validation -> handler : Handle StartSprintCommand
    handler -> db : BeginWorkspaceTransactionAsync (workspace lock); LoadSprintStartAsync:\nmode, Sprint with status, version and current memberships, active slot
    db --> handler : Current start conditions
    alt Sprint not found (or in another workspace)
      handler --> ctrl : 404; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (not found)
      client --> page : SprintStartView emits notFound; the dialog closes with Outdated; the opening page increments\nits counter and rereads its list, plan header or board, which shows its own state
    else Workspace in Kanban mode (L2-027.3)
      handler --> ctrl : 409 sprints paused; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (sprints paused)
      client --> page : blocked-kanban: the explanation fills the alert region and describes the dialog; focus moves to Close;\nno retry; SprintStartView emits modeChanged; the dialog closes with ModeChanged and the page calls\nProjectLayoutPage.modeChanged() (the planning page rereads its plan header)
    else Another sprint is Active (L2-023.2)
      handler --> ctrl : 409 naming the active sprint; neither sprint changes
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (active sprint exists)
      client --> page : blocked-active: the explanation naming the active sprint fills the alert region and describes\nthe dialog; focus moves to Review and close Sprint 8; Close; no retry
      opt Review and close Sprint 8
        actor -> page : Choose Review and close Sprint 8
        page -> page : SprintStartView emits closeSprintRequested(SprintReference from the 409); the dialog closes with\nCloseSprint; SprintsPage, SprintPlanningPage or SprintBoardPage calls openCloseSprint(sprintId)\nand CloseSprintDialog opens for that sprint (close-sprint)
      end
    else Sprint already Active or Closed (L2-023.4)
      handler --> ctrl : 409 not planned; history unchanged
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (not planned)
      client --> page : not-planned: the alert region names the current state and describes the dialog; focus moves\nto Close; no retry. SprintStartView emits outdated, so Close returns Outdated and the opening page\nrereads its list, plan header or board
    else Stale sprint version
      handler --> ctrl : 409 changed since reviewed; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (stale version)
      client --> page : Read the sprint once; stale state: neutral "Sprint 9 changed after you opened it",\nrefreshed summary; Start sprint asks again; no resubmission
    else Startable Planned sprint
      handler -> entity : L2-023 start(at, actorId): Active; record start instant, start actor,\ninitial-scope rows as tracked children
      entity --> handler : Active sprint with immutable initial scope
      handler -> db : L2-039 / L2-040 AddActiveSprintSlot; AddBoardState with its placements; AddAuditEvent;\nSaveChangesAsync: sprint, initial-scope rows, unique active slot, board, success audit in one transaction
      alt Active-slot unique violation (concurrent start, L2-041.2)
        db --> handler : Roll back everything
        handler --> ctrl : 409 naming the active sprint; neither sprint changes
        ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (active sprint exists)
        client --> page : blocked-active explanation naming the active sprint; focus moves to Review and close,\nwhich closes the dialog with CloseSprint(SprintReference); no retry
      else Commit fails
        db --> handler : Roll back business state and success audit
        handler --> ctrl : Generic 500 with correlation ID
        ctrl --> client : Failure; no successful-start claim
        client --> page : Failed state with reference ID; sprint still planned;\nStart sprint retries only when chosen
      else Commit succeeds
        db --> handler : Active sprint version
        handler --> ctrl : Started sprint
        ctrl --> client : 200 with sprint and version
        client --> page : SprintStartView emits started; the dialog closes with Started(SprintSaveResult); SprintsPage and\nSprintPlanningPage open the sprint board, SprintBoardPage increments its counter; the board heading takes focus
        page --> actor : The opening page shows the "Sprint 9 started" toast through TOAST_SERVICE
      end
    end
  end
end
note over ctrl, db
A workspace lock wait beyond the timeout returns 503 with Retry-After and no change;
the dialog shows the same failed state with the reference ID.
An unexpected 403 (access changed after sign-in) starts nothing; SprintStartView emits forbidden,
which the dialog relays as its own forbidden while it stays open, and the opening page shows
the "Your access changed" toast through TOAST_SERVICE, without Retry.
A start that gets no response is uncertain: the dialog says "We couldn't confirm whether Sprint 9
started." (no reference ID); SprintStartView emits unconfirmed, which the dialog relays while it
stays open, so the opening page rereads at once; the view reads the sprint once. Still Planned at
the same version offers Start sprint again; Active shows the neutral "Sprint 9 is active now."
(never "Nothing was changed") with Close only, which returns Outdated (unconfirmed-active).
SaveChangesAsync raises ConcurrencyConflictException on a stale version, mapped to the same 409.
Unexpected failures return generic 500 plus correlation ID (L2-043).
Diagnostics exclude secrets and contact payloads.
end note
@enduml
